##gff-version 3
# Biological RNA Editing Examples from NCBI RefSeq GRCh38.p14 (GCF_000001405.40)
#
# Context & Biological Mechanism:
# In standard eukaryotic reference annotations (NCBI RefSeq GFF3 / Ensembl), genomic
# CDS coordinates reflect the unedited genomic DNA sequence. Biological RNA editing
# (e.g. ADAR-mediated A-to-I editing or APOBEC-mediated C-to-U editing) is post-transcriptional.
# Therefore, direct in silico translation of these genomic CDS features generates the
# unedited precursor peptide, whereas downstream protein products (documented in RefSeq protein /
# GenPept records) contain the edited amino acids.
#
# 1. GRIA2 (Glutamate Ionotropic Receptor AMPA Type Subunit 2) - GeneID:2891, Chr 4 (+)
#    - Canonical A-to-I editing by ADAR2:
#      * Q/R site: Codon 607 (CAG -> CGG), converting Glutamine (Q) to Arginine (R)
#        in the channel pore (M2 loop), controlling Ca2+ permeability.
#        Genomic position: NC_000004.12:157336723 (A -> G / I in transcript).
#      * R/G site: Codon 764 (AGA -> GGA), converting Arginine (R) to Glycine (G)
#        in the ligand-binding domain (exon 13/14), affecting desensitization kinetics.
#    - Includes canonical isoform 1 (NM_000826.6 / NP_000817.5) and MANE Select isoform 2 (NM_001083619.3 / NP_001077088.2).
